## 4. Diagnosis

The count goes wrong in the `.list` branch of `generateSchemaFromNodeStatic` in `zig-parquet/src/core/writer.zig`, not in the DynamicWriter loop. `DynamicWriter.buildSerializedFooter` (dynamic_writer.zig:1543-1545) just calls the helper and advances `idx` correctly. Lines 1264 and 1287 of writer.zig, shown below:

```
1264:                const num_element_children = try countStructChildren(element);
...
1272:                    .num_children = 1,           // "items" LIST group: correct
...
1282:                schema[idx] = .{
1283:                    .type_ = null,
1284:                    .type_length = null,
1285:                    .repetition_type = .repeated,
1286:                    .name = "list",
1287:                    .num_children = num_element_children,
```

`countStructChildren` (writer.zig:1392-1398) returns the struct's field count for a struct element:

```
1392:    fn countStructChildren(node: *const SchemaNode) WriterError!i32 {
1393:        return switch (node.*) {
1394:            .optional => |child| countStructChildren(child),
1395:            .struct_ => |s| safe.castTo(i32, s.fields.len),
1396:            else => 1,
1397:        };
1398:    }
```

So for `list<struct{a,b}>` the "list" repeated group gets `s.fields.len` = 2. Per the Parquet layout the writer itself emits next (`generateSchemaFromNodeStatic(..., "element", element, .required)` at line 1296), the repeated "list" group should have exactly one child, the element group. The `else => 1` arm already gives the right value for primitive elements. The struct arm is the wrong one, and it is the same value that the element group itself should carry (2), which is why the file shows 2 under both "list" and "element".

Why the standalone case passes: I did not verify this. My hypothesis is that the walker in `buildTopInfos` runs `SchemaNode.buildFromElements` per top-level column, so a list group claiming 2 children swallows the following sibling `flag` as its second child and then runs past the end of the schema at line 792. With no following column, the extra count is never reached. Confirming this would need reading `SchemaNode.buildFromElements` in `zig-parquet/src/core/schema.zig`.

